WEBVTT

00:00.280 --> 00:04.120
For real, Blurin, that was really rough.

00:04.870 --> 00:09.220
We were suddenly summoned to the castle 
as soon as we got back from the battle.

00:09.220 --> 00:13.820
I was told we were getting a 
reward from King Lloyd, but...

00:14.500 --> 00:18.790
I'd never been in front of so many 
people before. I was so nervous!

00:19.310 --> 00:22.240
And the captain smacked me in the middle
of the ceremony for some reason...

00:22.240 --> 00:25.690
But to be honest, I was kinda happy.

00:26.510 --> 00:30.780
I never got any kind of award
 back in my old world.

00:31.820 --> 00:37.000
Anyway, Blurin, did you gain 
weight while I was gone?

00:40.080 --> 00:42.600
I mean, no matter how you look at it...

00:43.840 --> 00:46.240
Hey! There you are, Usato.

00:46.240 --> 00:48.510
Gomul? What's up?

00:48.510 --> 00:52.860
Someone from the castle dropped by
 and asked for you to pay a visit.

00:52.860 --> 00:55.290
Huh? Again? Why?

00:55.290 --> 00:58.030
Well, better get over there sooner than later.

00:58.030 --> 00:59.740
Sounded like they were in a hurry.

01:00.560 --> 01:04.590
Oh, but be careful if you're 
cutting through town.

01:04.590 --> 01:06.390
Huh? What do you mean?

01:07.320 --> 01:08.950
Who can say?

01:12.660 --> 01:14.050
Wh-What's all this?!

01:14.050 --> 01:15.510
He's a member of the Rescue Team!

01:14.470 --> 01:17.050
W-Wait, everyone! Please calm down!

01:15.510 --> 01:17.050
Thank you for saving my son!

01:17.050 --> 01:18.470
Take these with you!

01:18.470 --> 01:19.750
N-No, I couldn't!

01:19.750 --> 01:22.560
I c-can't carry that much!

01:20.180 --> 01:22.560
Now, don't hold back!

01:22.560 --> 01:24.510
U-Um, thank you very much...

01:23.620 --> 01:25.420
Go on, just take it!

01:40.530 --> 01:45.200
<i>The Wrong Way to Use Healing Magic</i>

02:56.190 --> 03:00.280
#12 The True Face of the Black Knight!

02:56.390 --> 03:00.270
Wow, you went through all that?
I'd expect no less, Sir Usato.

03:00.590 --> 03:03.670
No, no. It was hard to get
 away from the crowd.

03:04.760 --> 03:08.380
Well, I'm not at all surprised, 
considering your role in the battle.

03:09.190 --> 03:11.410
I'd like to thank you again.

03:11.410 --> 03:15.250
You have my gratitude for saving my comrades.

03:15.250 --> 03:20.180
Please stop! The knights also saved me
 plenty of times on the battlefield.

03:20.180 --> 03:25.090
And you protected the Rescue Team, too.
We all just did our part.

03:26.870 --> 03:30.200
You're such an interesting man, Sir Usato.

03:30.200 --> 03:34.260
I'll be counting on you again 
if I ever need a bodyguard.

03:36.760 --> 03:37.410
Of course!

03:37.410 --> 03:39.560
You've got a great eye, Sir Usato!

03:39.560 --> 03:42.420
Aruku is skilled in both magic and the sword!

03:42.420 --> 03:45.490
He could join the royal 
knights if he wanted to!

03:46.670 --> 03:48.480
Come on, Thomas!

03:48.480 --> 03:52.660
It's the truth. Please continue 
to utilize his services!

03:52.660 --> 03:54.540
Yes, of course!

03:55.190 --> 03:57.290
I-I appreciate it...

03:58.720 --> 04:02.040
My apologies for calling 
you back so soon, Usato.

04:02.420 --> 04:04.880
I was hoping you'd lend us your strength.

04:04.880 --> 04:06.810
Of course. What can I do for you?

04:07.680 --> 04:08.820
Siglis.

04:08.820 --> 04:09.490
Sire.

04:10.960 --> 04:14.780
We would like your help 
interrogating the Black Knight,

04:14.780 --> 04:16.850
whom you captured.

04:16.850 --> 04:18.310
<i>That girl?</i>

04:22.810 --> 04:26.720
What happened? Has she been 
violent during questioning?

04:26.720 --> 04:32.490
No, it seems she does not hold much 
loyalty to the Demon Lord's army.

04:32.490 --> 04:34.410
She's been answering us willingly.

04:34.410 --> 04:35.440
Then...

04:35.440 --> 04:40.670
However, we've yet to get the most 
critical intel we need out of her.

04:41.090 --> 04:45.410
We'd like to know the magic system of 
the commanding officers and their powers.

04:45.410 --> 04:47.500
Oh, I see.

04:47.500 --> 04:51.590
She claims she'll cooperate 
if we meet her demand.

04:56.170 --> 04:58.770
She wishes to see you, Sir Usato.

05:00.470 --> 05:01.780
Huh?

05:02.180 --> 05:04.120
Don't worry, Usato-kun!

05:04.120 --> 05:05.940
I volunteered to accompany you!

05:05.940 --> 05:08.480
I'll protect you if she tries anything!

05:08.480 --> 05:13.080
Uh, I heard that the Black 
Knight is being cooperative.

05:13.080 --> 05:16.730
Plus, you already lost to her once...

05:17.360 --> 05:23.360
Well, that's true. Only you or Captain Rose 
would stand a chance against her...

05:23.360 --> 05:25.560
But I can at least be a meat shield!

05:25.560 --> 05:28.020
Th-Thank you for saying so.

05:28.630 --> 05:33.050
I wonder why I was able to hold my 
own against her in the first place.

05:33.280 --> 05:37.540
The Black Knight has an
 affinity for dark magic.

05:37.540 --> 05:42.220
It appears that magic was completely 
canceled out by your healing magic.

05:42.220 --> 05:44.880
I see. We offset each other, huh?

05:44.880 --> 05:46.900
Wait, doesn't that mean...

05:47.170 --> 05:53.990
Was the healing magic I was casting
with each punch negated, too?

05:55.110 --> 05:56.860
Yes, that stands to reason.

05:57.280 --> 05:58.720
Commander Siglis!

05:58.720 --> 06:01.060
Has the Black Knight 
received medical attention?

06:01.060 --> 06:01.870
Huh?

06:01.870 --> 06:06.330
No, she's had her black armor on ever 
since she regained consciousness.

06:06.880 --> 06:08.370
Oh, no!

06:10.440 --> 06:11.300
Hey!

06:13.630 --> 06:15.310
You're hurt, aren't you?

06:15.310 --> 06:16.980
And pretty bad, I bet!

06:18.460 --> 06:19.970
You're here...

06:19.970 --> 06:24.140
My attacks... 
You took all those punches directly.

06:24.140 --> 06:28.080
I'm not trying to brag,
 but my fists can shatter even rocks.

06:28.080 --> 06:30.000
I know you're hurt bad.

06:31.340 --> 06:33.860
Yeah, that's right.

06:34.200 --> 06:37.890
But it doesn't matter. This is 
what pain feels like, isn't it?

06:40.430 --> 06:41.610
Usato-kun...

06:42.370 --> 06:44.140
She's a hardcore M.

06:44.140 --> 06:46.540
Please shut up for a second.

06:50.020 --> 06:54.140
You wanted to see me. Why?

06:55.650 --> 07:04.110
I guess I just wanted to see the face of 
the guy who messed me up so badly again...

07:06.820 --> 07:10.170
Commander Siglis, please let me in.

07:10.170 --> 07:11.480
What? But...

07:11.480 --> 07:14.400
Please. I have to help her.

07:25.410 --> 07:26.580
Give me your hand.

07:26.580 --> 07:28.500
For what? Torture?

07:28.500 --> 07:30.640
I told you to give me your hand!

07:33.040 --> 07:36.010
Wh-What are you trying to do?!

07:36.010 --> 07:38.070
That's obvious. I'm going to heal you.

07:38.930 --> 07:40.340
There's no need.

07:40.340 --> 07:43.110
Let me go! Let me go!

07:48.980 --> 07:52.110
It'd leave a bad taste in 
my mouth if I let you die.

07:52.110 --> 07:53.710
Shut up and let me heal you.

07:55.360 --> 07:57.530
What is this?

08:10.660 --> 08:12.190
It's so warm...

08:12.960 --> 08:14.250
Usato-kun?

08:14.250 --> 08:16.030
It's all right, I think.

08:19.510 --> 08:20.600
All done.

08:23.560 --> 08:26.490
Um, can you let go now?

08:26.490 --> 08:28.190
Just a little longer.

08:36.360 --> 08:39.970
I've never felt this before.

08:40.940 --> 08:43.870
I want to stay like this a little longer...

08:48.120 --> 08:51.950
How can I say no when you 
ask me looking like that?

08:53.130 --> 08:57.050
<i>The Wrong Way to Use Healing Magic</i>

08:57.920 --> 08:59.220
Now, then...

08:59.220 --> 09:02.640
I'll be training you personally today.

09:02.640 --> 09:05.800
Uh, may I ask why?

09:05.800 --> 09:09.040
Like I said before, the Demon Lord's 
army <i>will</i> attack again.

09:09.040 --> 09:13.200
There are some things I want you 
to learn so you'll be prepared.

09:13.620 --> 09:14.850
I see.

09:14.850 --> 09:18.600
I do want to level up my healing magic.

09:18.600 --> 09:21.210
I still can't treat complicated 
things like sickness...

09:21.210 --> 09:23.720
There are steps for accomplishing that.

09:23.720 --> 09:25.820
It's out of reach for you right now.

09:25.820 --> 09:26.840
What?

09:26.840 --> 09:29.080
So, more physical training?

09:29.080 --> 09:33.530
No. Your endurance and physicality 
are just barely over the acceptable line,

09:33.530 --> 09:35.460
so we won't worry about that for now.

09:35.990 --> 09:37.880
Then what are we going to do?

09:39.430 --> 09:40.680
Um...

09:41.930 --> 09:43.340
Captain?

09:45.470 --> 09:48.530
I'm going to punch you.

09:48.520 --> 09:49.980
<b>...Huh?</b>

09:49.180 --> 09:49.990
Huh?

09:49.980 --> 09:54.530
<i>RUMBLE</i>

09:49.980 --> 09:54.530
<i>RUMBLE</i>

09:49.990 --> 09:53.630
I'm going to punch you 
faster than you can react.

09:53.630 --> 09:54.520
Dodge.

09:54.520 --> 09:56.680
Whoa! You actually hate me, don't you?!

09:56.680 --> 09:59.000
I'll straight-up explode if you punch me!

09:59.250 --> 10:02.110
You rely too much on your healing magic.

10:02.410 --> 10:05.380
Of course, I <i>am</i> the one 
who trained you that way.

10:05.380 --> 10:08.760
It just means it's time to 
move to the next step.

10:08.760 --> 10:11.840
No! I'm gonna be murdered!

10:12.170 --> 10:15.070
You think you can just heal 
yourself if you get hurt, right?

10:16.280 --> 10:21.210
But healing magic won't work on wounds
made by weapons that curse the wound.

10:21.650 --> 10:23.610
You need to learn to dodge.

10:24.250 --> 10:28.160
Hey, I'm no monster. I'll start light.

10:28.160 --> 10:30.980
You shouldn't punch your subordinates, 
lightly or otherwise!

10:30.980 --> 10:32.790
You're messed up in the head!

10:32.790 --> 10:34.940
Er, I'm sorry...

10:34.940 --> 10:37.840
I see. So you want me to be serious.

10:37.840 --> 10:42.000
I'm thrilled you're so passionate
 about your training!

10:52.570 --> 10:54.140
You'd better not block.

10:54.140 --> 10:55.760
This is so unfair!

11:10.760 --> 11:12.640
What a nightmare.

11:12.640 --> 11:14.820
Have I been training too much?

11:14.820 --> 11:18.000
Of course. There was no 
sudden practice exercise at all.

11:18.000 --> 11:21.030
You're awake. Let's go again.

11:21.030 --> 11:23.230
<i>I shouldn't run away from reality...</i>

11:23.230 --> 11:26.080
Don't worry. I held back earlier.

11:26.080 --> 11:27.670
You're holding up fine, right?

11:29.170 --> 11:30.870
Thank you, ma'am...

11:34.090 --> 11:36.490
We've been at it for three whole days!

11:36.490 --> 11:38.090
Isn't my captain the worst?

11:38.090 --> 11:41.500
If I get close to dodging, 
she just throws punches even faster.

11:41.500 --> 11:46.130
Yesterday, when I was focused on dodging, 
she went and landed a critical hit on me...

11:46.130 --> 11:49.090
Don't you think she's kinda 
losing the point of our training?

11:50.120 --> 11:51.470
Hey...

11:51.470 --> 11:54.000
You just start spouting off 
the moment you show up?

11:54.000 --> 11:55.770
What are you even here for?

11:55.770 --> 12:00.340
Well, my captain suddenly had something
to do, so there's no training today.

12:00.820 --> 12:03.150
And I was wondering how you were doing.

12:03.470 --> 12:05.560
Can't you tell just by looking?

12:05.560 --> 12:07.850
What are you going to do from now on?

12:08.720 --> 12:12.740
That's not for me to decide
 in my current predicament.

12:12.740 --> 12:15.050
Yeah, I guess not.

12:16.550 --> 12:18.330
What do you...

12:21.350 --> 12:22.720
It's nothing.

12:23.700 --> 12:25.430
Now get out of here already.

12:25.430 --> 12:28.480
Yeah, yeah. Got it.

12:36.570 --> 12:37.830
Your Majesty.

12:38.580 --> 12:39.910
You called for me?

12:40.480 --> 12:42.830
Thank you for coming, Rose.

12:42.830 --> 12:46.740
There are two things I'd like to ask of you.

12:46.740 --> 12:48.770
I'm at your service.

13:06.590 --> 13:07.930
Oh, Sir Usato!

13:08.250 --> 13:10.050
Hello, Princess Celia.

13:10.050 --> 13:12.370
Looks like Kazuki's up to 
something interesting.

13:12.370 --> 13:13.350
Yes.

13:13.350 --> 13:17.770
He wanted to improve his magic 
and began training like so.

13:18.500 --> 13:21.900
I've been cautioning him not 
to overexert himself...

13:22.490 --> 13:23.730
<i>Huh?</i>

13:23.730 --> 13:26.550
<i>Is this what training is supposed to be like?</i>

13:29.970 --> 13:32.530
Sir Usato, that's a rather scary face...

13:33.560 --> 13:35.490
Oh, Usato!

13:37.790 --> 13:42.710
I heard from Senpai that you 
made the Black Knight cry.

13:42.710 --> 13:45.190
Huh? I didn't do anything weird to her!

13:45.190 --> 13:47.220
I just healed her wounds!

13:47.220 --> 13:49.890
I know. I'm just teasing you.

13:50.180 --> 13:51.580
Jeez...

13:51.580 --> 13:54.960
There was something else 
that Dame Suzune said.

13:54.960 --> 13:59.370
She said you'd triggered a... "flag"...
with the Black Knight, as well?

13:59.370 --> 14:04.220
Princess, there's no need to take 
anything she says seriously.

14:05.670 --> 14:09.060
By the way, I heard that they were 
able to collect the information

14:09.060 --> 14:11.300
they needed on the 
Demon Lord's army from her.

14:11.300 --> 14:13.620
My father was most grateful.

14:13.620 --> 14:15.640
Oh, is that so?

14:15.640 --> 14:19.260
His trust in you only continues to grow.

14:20.400 --> 14:22.490
I heard that if you hadn't been

14:22.490 --> 14:26.380
on the battlefield that day,
 there's a real possibility we'd have lost.

14:26.380 --> 14:28.220
No, that's not true...

14:28.220 --> 14:29.890
It's completely true.

14:29.890 --> 14:33.050
If you hadn't saved me, I'd be d—

14:33.050 --> 14:34.280
Whoops!

14:34.800 --> 14:38.210
N-Nothing. I should get back to training.

14:40.640 --> 14:42.050
See you later!

14:42.050 --> 14:43.750
I'll come visit you again!

14:43.750 --> 14:45.580
Do take care!

14:46.230 --> 14:48.770
Right, time to train!

14:50.410 --> 14:55.610
Before that, Sir Kazuki, I'd like to ask you
 for details about what you just said.

14:56.330 --> 15:01.920
If Sir Usato hadn't saved you,
you would be... what, exactly?

15:01.920 --> 15:04.290
U-Uh, what was I going to say?

15:04.290 --> 15:06.000
May I know the details?

15:08.210 --> 15:09.800
S-Sorry!

15:09.800 --> 15:14.540
<i>Kazuki probably hid the fact that the Black 
Knight almost killed him from the princess.</i>

15:16.040 --> 15:19.330
<i>But I wonder what's going 
to happen to her now.</i>

15:19.330 --> 15:21.360
<i>She gave up the info they wanted, so...</i>

15:22.740 --> 15:25.550
<i>They wouldn't execute 
her or anything, right?</i>

15:28.440 --> 15:30.580
<i>That guy named Usato...</i>

15:30.580 --> 15:33.230
<i>What is he trying to do?</i>

15:33.230 --> 15:35.110
<i>Why did he bother coming to see me?</i>

15:36.760 --> 15:37.790
<i>Usato?</i>

15:42.920 --> 15:43.930
<i>No!</i>

15:45.080 --> 15:46.390
Hey there.

15:48.260 --> 15:51.420
<i>She's in the same uniform as Usato. 
Is she the captain he spoke of?</i>

15:52.120 --> 15:55.220
This is the first time we've 
met while you were awake.

15:55.220 --> 16:00.600
Not that I'd be here if His Majesty
 hadn't asked me to be.

16:00.600 --> 16:02.010
Why are you here?

16:02.010 --> 16:04.440
You have two options.

16:06.110 --> 16:09.980
The first is to spend the rest 
of your life in this prison cell.

16:09.980 --> 16:11.940
And the second...

16:11.940 --> 16:13.620
Kill me if you must.

16:13.620 --> 16:17.030
Don't rush things. So impatient.

16:21.950 --> 16:26.690
Your second option is honestly
 a ton of trouble for me.

16:27.330 --> 16:31.110
It's taking you under my wing and 
turning you into an upright human,

16:29.590 --> 16:30.960
<b>Upright Human</b>

16:29.590 --> 16:30.960
<b>Upright Human</b>

16:30.960 --> 16:33.550
<b>Upright Demon</b>

16:31.110 --> 16:33.550
or rather, an upright demon.

16:33.540 --> 16:34.590
Huh?

16:34.590 --> 16:36.300
What are you saying? Are you stup—

16:38.980 --> 16:40.050
I see.

16:40.050 --> 16:42.650
Healing magic really works on you.

16:40.060 --> 16:42.640
<b>Wobble</b>

16:40.060 --> 16:42.640
<b>Wobble</b>

16:43.350 --> 16:46.540
His Majesty dislikes killing prisoners of war.

16:47.060 --> 16:50.220
Even troublesome ones like you.

16:51.890 --> 16:56.060
Also, I know just how much demonkind 
cares about their comrades.

16:56.370 --> 16:59.720
If we kill a prisoner of war, 
they'll be outraged.

16:59.720 --> 17:03.510
And enemies burning with the desire 
for revenge are the worst to deal with.

17:14.170 --> 17:15.460
My mana?

17:15.460 --> 17:17.350
That's a magic tool that seals mana.

17:17.350 --> 17:18.500
What?!

17:18.500 --> 17:21.940
Should you be using something 
so valuable this nonchalantly?!

17:21.940 --> 17:24.880
We could watch over you in prison,

17:24.880 --> 17:28.740
but it'd be a waste of the kingdom's 
resources to do that forever.

17:28.740 --> 17:32.140
So it looks like turning you into
 an upright demon is the way to go.

17:32.140 --> 17:33.110
Huh?

17:33.110 --> 17:34.570
Didn't you say I had a choice?!

17:34.570 --> 17:39.660
His Majesty told me he was leaving you to me.

17:40.740 --> 17:43.400
No! What are you planning to do?!

17:43.400 --> 17:45.870
You're in no position to refuse.

17:53.180 --> 17:55.080
Good job, Blurin!

17:55.080 --> 17:58.240
At this rate, you'll slim down in no time!

17:59.110 --> 18:00.670
Okay, one more lap!

18:01.280 --> 18:03.560
Didn't I tell you to take today off?

18:03.560 --> 18:06.480
Well, I felt a little restless...

18:07.040 --> 18:09.240
But is that any reason to kick someone?

18:10.350 --> 18:11.460
What's that?

18:11.460 --> 18:13.500
Oh, this thing?

18:16.800 --> 18:18.200
What?! Isn't that—

18:18.200 --> 18:19.230
Shut up!

18:19.230 --> 18:20.410
So unreasonable!

18:20.660 --> 18:23.630
Wh-Why the heck did you bring her here?!

18:23.630 --> 18:28.690
Starting today, I'm going to reform her 
as an errand runner for the Rescue Team.

18:28.690 --> 18:31.500
It'll be fun to train a demon.

18:31.500 --> 18:33.360
Wait, wait, wait... But...

18:33.360 --> 18:36.840
Her magic's been sealed, so no need to
worry about her trying anything funny.

18:37.550 --> 18:39.090
And...

18:39.090 --> 18:42.470
I'll be supervising her training for a while.

18:42.470 --> 18:44.860
Just like I did with you.

18:44.860 --> 18:46.880
Are you serious?

18:52.160 --> 18:53.810
Where am I?

18:54.950 --> 18:56.790
Oh, Usato?

18:57.750 --> 18:59.460
My condolences.

18:59.890 --> 19:00.610
Huh?

19:05.550 --> 19:06.440
Come in.

19:08.590 --> 19:09.980
Excuse me.

19:09.980 --> 19:10.880
Hey.

19:11.270 --> 19:13.730
How's the newbie?

19:13.730 --> 19:19.320
She had some complaints, but she calmed 
down a bit after taking a bath.

19:20.220 --> 19:22.600
I think she's currently asleep in her room.

19:22.600 --> 19:23.760
I see.

19:25.560 --> 19:29.920
Sounds like she still doesn't 
understand the situation she's in.

19:29.920 --> 19:33.350
Well, she'll grasp it 
once she starts training.

19:33.350 --> 19:35.110
I'm sure she will.

19:35.110 --> 19:37.310
So, what business did you have with me?

19:37.310 --> 19:42.030
Oh, I spoke directly with His Majesty today.

19:43.240 --> 19:45.890
It concerned you, as well.

19:47.960 --> 19:52.600
Rose, I hope to form alliances with 
other countries to stand against

19:52.600 --> 19:55.120
the threat that is the Demon Lord's army.

19:56.810 --> 20:01.540
I'd like to send representatives 
to various nations with a missive.

20:03.010 --> 20:06.320
A journey to deliver missives?

20:06.670 --> 20:10.600
That's right. The representatives 
 His Majesty has chosen are

20:10.600 --> 20:13.550
Hero Suzune, Hero Kazuki, and...

20:14.240 --> 20:16.440
You, Usato.

20:17.430 --> 20:18.270
Huh?!

20:18.270 --> 20:22.190
I get Senpai and Kazuki, but why me?!

20:22.190 --> 20:23.430
Isn't it obvious?

20:23.430 --> 20:27.320
His Majesty believes you could
successfully complete this mission,

20:27.320 --> 20:29.820
which the fate of the 
whole kingdom depends on.

20:30.560 --> 20:32.350
I share his opinion.

20:33.460 --> 20:35.760
There's still some time before you leave.

20:36.130 --> 20:37.930
Get ready, Usato.

20:37.930 --> 20:38.830
Right.

20:42.160 --> 20:43.920
Here ya go.

20:43.920 --> 20:45.540
Thank you very much.

20:46.070 --> 20:48.180
Um, Mr. Usato...

20:48.180 --> 20:51.280
Good luck with your work in the Rescue Team!

20:51.280 --> 20:53.590
That's all we wanted to say!

20:53.590 --> 20:54.740
Uh... Sure.

20:57.150 --> 20:59.610
Sorry about last time.

20:59.610 --> 21:02.050
We got too excited.

21:02.050 --> 21:04.500
We won't get carried away again.

21:04.890 --> 21:05.860
Okay...

21:08.930 --> 21:11.840
<i>The people of this kingdom are so kind...</i>

21:12.710 --> 21:17.520
<i>This journey to deliver missives
 is really to protect them.</i>

21:17.520 --> 21:19.380
Oh? Usato-kun?

21:20.550 --> 21:21.450
Oh.

21:21.450 --> 21:22.340
Senpai.

21:22.340 --> 21:24.630
What a coincidence running into you here!

21:24.910 --> 21:28.680
Why, this must be what they call fate!

21:28.680 --> 21:32.310
Yeah, I think there's just a pretty good 
chance of bumping into people at the market.

21:32.310 --> 21:37.010
I think you've just triggered
 another flag with me!

21:38.440 --> 21:40.950
I'm not following you at all.

21:44.560 --> 21:45.850
Little fox!

21:45.850 --> 21:46.820
I found you!

21:51.520 --> 21:53.460
I finally got you!

21:53.460 --> 21:55.190
We need to talk!

21:56.400 --> 22:00.050
I was waiting for you. 
It's time to pay me back.

22:00.050 --> 22:00.890
Huh?

22:01.200 --> 22:07.130
Healer... Save my mother.
